<div class="card mb-1">
    <h6 class="card-header d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center text-primary">
        <span><i class="mdi mdi-information-outline me-2"></i> TSC Avanced Security Shield Configuration Tips</span>
        <button class="btn btn-light btn-sm" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapseTips" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseTips">
            <i class="mdi mdi-chevron-down"></i>
        </button>
    </h6>
    <div id="collapseTips" class="collapse">
        <div class="card-body">
            <ul class="mb-0">
                <li><strong>RequestLimit</strong>: Max requests per user/session in the time window. <span class="text-muted">e.g. <code>100</code></span></li>
                <li><strong>TimeWindowSeconds</strong>: Time frame (in seconds) to count requests. <span class="text-muted">e.g. <code>60</code></span></li>
                <li><strong>BlockDurationMinutes</strong>: Time (in minutes) to block after abuse. <span class="text-muted">e.g. <code>15</code></span></li>
                <li><strong>IPRequestLimit</strong>: Max requests per IP in a separate window. <span class="text-muted">e.g. <code>300</code></span></li>
                <li><strong>IPTimeWindowSeconds</strong>: Interval (seconds) to evaluate per-IP abuse. <span class="text-muted">e.g. <code>60</code></span></li>
                <li><strong>WhitelistedHeaders</strong>: Trusted headers to skip limits. <span class="text-muted">e.g. <code>X-Internal-Request</code></span></li>
                <li><strong>WhiteListedCountriesCode</strong>: ISO country codes allowed to access the system. <span class="text-muted">Used for geolocation-based access filtering. e.g. <code>CM</code> for Cameroon, <code>NG</code> for Nigeria</span></li>
                <li><strong>CameroonCidrs</strong>: IP CIDRs allowed for system access from whitelisted countries. <span class="text-muted">Used to enforce IP-level geographic restrictions alongside country codes. <br />Example (single IP): <code>102.244.128.23/32</code> <br />Example (range): <code>102.244.128.0/18</code></span></li>
                <li><strong>SuspiciousIndicators</strong>: Keywords & filenames to flag/block. <span class="text-muted">e.g. <code>shell.php</code>, <code>wp-login</code></span></li>
                <li><strong>ExcludedPaths/Substrings/Extensions</strong>: Bypass routing for static/internal requests.</li>
                <li><strong>BadUserAgents</strong>: User-Agent signatures of known bots and attackers. <span class="text-muted">e.g. <code>curl</code>, <code>python-requests</code></span></li>
                <li><strong>Reset Policy</strong>: Deleting the current configuration will automatically initialize a secure default policy. <span class="text-muted">Used to recover or rebaseline protections. <strong>Note:</strong> This action will permanently remove all custom settings you have configured.</span></li>
            </ul>
        </div>


        <!-- Default Config Display -->
        <div class="alert alert-secondary mt-3">
            <strong>Sample Configuration Snapshot:</strong><br />
            <code>
                RequestLimit = 100<br />
                TimeWindowSeconds = 60<br />
                BlockDurationMinutes = 15<br />
                IPRequestLimit = 300<br />
                IPTimeWindowSeconds = 60<br />
                WhitelistedHeaders = ["FLUXTSC-Internal-Request", "FLUXTSC-Bypass-Limit"]<br />
                CameroonCidrs = ["102.244.128.0/18"]<br />
                SuspiciousIndicators = [...blocked filenames & attack tools...]<br />
                ExcludedPaths = ["/favicon.ico", "/Content/", ...]<br />
                BadUserAgents = ["curl", "python-requests"]
            </code>
        </div>
    </div>

</div>
